data: {"choices":[{"delta":{"reasoning_content":"Now I understand the structure:\n- `AppShell` renders a plain `\u003cdiv data-component=\"AppShell\"\u003e` with children — so the layout (header top, footer bottom, content centered) is up to my CSS plus the app-shell.css component sheet.\n- `Header` renders a `\u003cheader\u003e`, `Footer` a `\u003cfooter\u003e`.\n- Tokens `--color-cat-1`, `--color-cat-5`, `--color-cat-6` exist.\n\nLet me quickly peek at app-shell.css to understand what layout it gives (e.g., is AppShell a flex column with a main content area?). The design says \"The content area between them\" — AppShell's children will be Header, my content, Footer. I need to check whether app-shell.css already makes the shell a flex column filling the viewport. Let me look at the CSS classes cs-component-app-shell-24 (AppShell), -3 (Header), -20 (Footer)."},"finish_reason":null,"index":0,"raw_output":null}],"created":1793343002,"id":"chatcmpl-a42e1083","model":"accounts/fireworks/models/kimi-k3","object":"chat.completion.chunk","usage":null}

